SCOPE

The MIT licence above covers the platform code only:

    ctfbrain/    the indexer, search engine, CLI and web application
    ingest/      the ingestion pipelines
    tests/
    docs/
    Makefile, Dockerfile, docker-compose.yml, pyproject.toml

It does NOT cover the knowledge base contents.

CONTENT AND THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

Everything under content/ and vendor/ that was ingested, mirrored or vendored
belongs to its original authors and remains under its own licence. Each
document records where it came from:

  * ingested documents carry a `source:` link in their frontmatter
  * mirrored corpora also carry a `license:` field, and are listed in
    content/reference/ext-CORPORA-PROVENANCE.md with their commit and licence
  * vendored repositories keep their upstream LICENSE file, and are listed in
    vendor/PROVENANCE.md with their commit and licence

Two mirrored corpora are Creative Commons NonCommercial:

  * CTF Wiki (ctf-wiki/ctf-wiki)            CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
  * HackTricks (HackTricks-wiki/hacktricks) CC BY-NC 4.0

Because of those, THIS MIRROR MUST NOT BE REDISTRIBUTED COMMERCIALLY.

If you are an author and want your work removed, delete the file and run
`make index`.
